  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd the catalog case `2d/hole-work` on an original 90 x 90 x 20 mm plate.\nThe case has Drill, Bore, Circular, a tap drill and Thread operations.\nIt includes the generator, mesh, command script, embedded project, NC program and README.\nThe decision file records the choices and limits.\nEffort: medium.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no combined example for these hole operations.\nIssue #2862 requests this case for debugging and testing.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `hole_work_case_posts_drilling_cycles_and_thread_helix`.\nThe first run failed on unchanged code: `2d/hole-work: missing model/`.\nThe pin checks operation order, four bolt-circle G81 cycles, the tap drill and the thread pitch.\n\nMutations:\n\n- Remove the case folder: red. Restore it: green.\n- Replace G81 with G80: red. Restore the NC bytes: green.\n- Flatten the thread helix Z coordinates: red. Restore the NC bytes: green.\n\nThere is no new guard in product code. Removing the new case restores the upstream behavior.\n\nValidation on the final files:\n\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: green for all three cases.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, whole catalog suite.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main`: green.\n\nThe first clippy run found a chunk-iteration lint in the new pin. The final run passed after that fix.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nOne new file: `examples/catalog/2d/hole-work/hole-work.nc`, 297 lines.\nThe diff adds the five operations, their tool changes, cycles and arcs.\nNo existing NC or CL file changes.\nThe program shows four bolt-circle G81 cycles and one tap-drill G81 cycle.\nThe thread has three radial passes with G03 helix blocks at pitch 1.25.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo machine or control simulator ran the program.\nNo UI, screenshot, PDF, heavy lane, Windows or macOS check ran.\nThe tools have no modelled holders.\nThe fixture and spoil board are not modelled.\nThe README names the required clearance below the plate.\nThe drill point reaches Z-2.803. The bore reaches Z-1.\n\nA larger Circular cut produced blocking verification warnings.\nThe separate defect is #2898, linked on #2392 and #2862.\nThe committed example uses a smaller Circular cut that verifies without warnings.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2883 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nBoth PRs add separate functions in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`.\n#2877 also touched that file. It merged during this work.\nThis branch includes its changes from upstream/main ab9955105.\nThe case folders do not overlap.\n\nChangelog: Examples: add the hole-work catalog case with drilling cycles, boring, circular milling and an M8 x 1.25 thread helix.\n\nFixes #2862\n",
